                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d061ea16-e786-3e98-924c-090f3bbd42f0",
                                        "entry_id": "923f587f-22d2-3b3b-b1be-dccf8aa80d56",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who uses a parachute; a parachutist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb8c710f-9f71-4cb7-944f-76f04db851af",
                                                "sense_id": "d061ea16-e786-3e98-924c-090f3bbd42f0",
                                                "text": "If you want to coordinate your bathing, beach walks and concession and boardwalk excursions with the show, keep in mind that the Army’s Golden Knights parachute team is scheduled to come by at 10:28; the Navy Leap Frogs parachuters at 11:16 and a B-1 bomber at 11:48."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fb7b70c9-fd14-49ae-8121-16e718ec8735",
                        "source_entry_id": "2cf2325c-8661-3d07-b668-9283965a173c",
                        "target_lang_word": "parachutist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "parachutist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d3445f3c-d081-3668-885b-271a8dacd4fb",
                                        "entry_id": "62a4667d-3299-3f30-b45f-3dc006656c52",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who jumps from an aircraft using a parachute, especially as a sport."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2452500e-908e-4ecc-90ea-ef33d9707641",
                                                "sense_id": "d3445f3c-d081-3668-885b-271a8dacd4fb",
                                                "text": "If any of the extreme sports can be considered truly high risk, then B.A.S.E. Jumping is that sport. […] Modern B.A.S.E. jumping is believed to have started in 1978, where daring parachutists first began jumping off of El Capitan, a 3,000 foot (915m) cliff high above Yosemite National Park."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f21d26b2-a14d-4d95-ba85-c55c37b6d090",
                                                "sense_id": "d3445f3c-d081-3668-885b-271a8dacd4fb",
                                                "text": "I waited and he came to the point: he wanted me simply to talk to a patient he had inherited, a sports parachutist who had Roman Candled into a tree and broken and disarticulated his back."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff9130b4-d3b8-421c-9dab-15533634d195",
                                                "sense_id": "d3445f3c-d081-3668-885b-271a8dacd4fb",
                                                "text": "Some hit the rocky outcrops\n Some fell into the sea\n Some even 'Roman Candled'\n (A parachutist I would never be)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
